  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_014, acc=0.725) is the best configuration by a wide margin over all scgpt-based runs (~0.52). The only untested variable within this top-performing regime is the fusion method: we have only tested 'weighted' with scvi_n200+ViT-L. Config_036 changes only the fusion from weighted to concat, directly testing whether the fusion mechanism matters when the RNA encoder is strong. With scgpt, weighted (0.520) barely beat concat (0.507), but that regime was overall weak; the dynamics may differ with scvi_n200. Resolving this single-variable question is critical before spending remaining budget on other axes (aggregation, image encoder), because it determines the architectural template for any further exploitation. With 4 experiments left, locking down the best fusion for the top encoder pair is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step."
}

